{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Go down and you shall come up, etc., with you.</b> He doubled the saying <b>go, descend</b> — once for its own sake and once to speak to him language of descent. Or perhaps the descent is because previously Moses had no bounded place on the mountain and would ascend to the top of the mountain, and when he refused, He said to him <b>go down and you shall come up</b> etc. — meaning: just as Aharon has a boundary, so too you have a boundary. And this is what He said ״עִמָּךְ״ — behold, He equated the brothers in the matter of boundary."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:24.455877208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}